   "summary": "President Lee Jae Myung was set to depart Monday on a four-day trip to attend an Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN) summit in the Philippines and an Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation (APEC) summit in China. During the ASEAN summit beginning Monday in Manila, the South Korean president will participate in a South Korea-ASEAN summit to discuss cooperation with the region, followed by a summit with leaders of the five Mekong countries — Cambodia, Laos, Myanmar, Thailand and Vietnam.",
   "summary_zh": "李在明总统定于周一启程，开启为期四天的行程，前往菲律宾出席东南亚国家联盟（ASEAN）峰会，并赴中国出席亚太经济合作组织（APEC）峰会。在周一于马尼拉开幕的东盟峰会上，韩国总统将参加韩国—东盟峰会，讨论与该地区的合作，随后与湄公河五国领导人举行峰会——柬埔寨、老挝、缅甸、泰国和越南。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "President Lee Jae Myung was set to depart Monday on a four-day trip to attend an Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN) summit in the Philippines and an Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation (APEC) summit in China. During the ASEAN summit beginning Monday in Manila, the South Korean president will participate in a South Korea-ASEAN summit to discuss cooperation with the region, followed by a summit with leaders of the five Mekong countries — Cambodia, Laos, Myanmar, Thailand and Vietnam. The following day, he will attend an ASEAN Plus Three summit, bringing together leaders from ASEAN member countries, South Korea, China and Japan, as well as an East Asia Summit involving 16 countries in East Asia. On the sidelines of the two summits, Lee is also expected to hold bilateral talks with participating leaders, including Thai Prime Minister Anutin Charnvirakul and Philippine President Ferdinand Romualdez Marcos Jr., both later Monday. The president also plans to call on ASEAN and APEC member countries to support Seoul's peaceful coexistence policy toward North Korea and convey a \"positive message\" in favor of peace and security on the Korean Peninsula, the official noted",
